<title>FRANCE: PARIS BOURSE.</title>
<headline>PARIS BOURSE.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>French shares were seen slipping in thin trade with technical indications suggesting a further consolidation despite a firm undertone, dealers said.</p>
<p>Credit Agricole futures said that 2,908 would be an objective with intermediate support at 2,922. If shares resumed their rise resistance would be at 2,951 and 2,972, it said.</p>
<p>Bouygues trades ex-dividend today.</p>
<p>Eurotunnel executive chairman Patrick Ponsolle said on Sunday that the company was cleared by a judicial inquiry from responsibility for a November fire which caused severe damage.</p>
